{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>If as a thanksgiving.</b> Its sense: that he give thanks to HaShem that he escaped from trouble." "<b>Cakes of unleavened bread.</b> As he wishes, but no fewer than two. And likewise for the thin unleavened wafers." "<b>Soaked.</b> The preferred interpretation in my eyes is that it is choice, and the unleavened cakes and wafers are baked, but the cake of the soaked is not so."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:08:54.241447464Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}